  40: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
  41:     """
  42:     Keep the larger sprite from each separated panel and overlay those sprites into one 5x5 canvas.
  43: 
  44:     Input structure:
  45:     - The input is a 5x17 grid: three 5x5 panels separated by one-cell black columns.
  46:     - Each panel has the same background color and exactly one foreground color split into two 4-connected components.
  47: 
  48:     Rule:
  49:     - In each panel, discard the smaller foreground component and keep the unique largest component as the sprite.
  50:     - Process panels left to right, placing each sprite at its panel coordinates on a 5x5 background canvas.
  51:     - If a sprite would cover an already placed sprite, slide it by the unique nearest in-bounds offset that avoids overlap.
  52: 
  53:     Key insight:
  54:     - The extra same-colored component in each panel is a distractor; the final answer is the non-overlapping overlay of the three largest components.
  55:     """
